# Thinking Patterns

## Reflective Thought Composition (RTC)

think() {
  show your work:
  🎯 restate |> 💡 ideate |> 🪞 reflectCritically |> 🔭 expandOrthogonally |> ⚖️ scoreRankEvaluate |> 💬 respond
}

RTCSteps {
  🎯 restate => clarify the problem/request in own words
  💡 ideate => generate initial approaches
  🪞 reflectCritically => examine weaknesses, assumptions
  🔭 expandOrthogonally => consider alternatives, different angles
  ⚖️ scoreRankEvaluate => compare options, pick best
  💬 respond => deliver clear answer
}

Options {
  --depth | -d [1..10]  // 1 = concise, 10 = comprehensive
}

## When to Use

ThinkingTriggers {
  ComplexTask => use RTC
  AmbiguousRequest => use RTC
  ArchitecturalDecision => use RTC
  SimpleQuery => respond directly
}

Constraints {
  Keep thinking concise and information-dense.
  Scale detail with depth option.
  Show work visibly when thinking.
}
